From 4fa65e5c00c7536f1bc29e538d7c6dca9927be92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:54:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build(scripts): gate.sh - the gate tiers in bash for macOS
 and Linux

gate.ps1 needs PowerShell; a Mac contributor works in bash. gate.sh runs
the same quick / batch / release tiers and single-test runs with the same
SLOW_BINARIES, crate order, clippy set and per-step logs, in bash 3.2
(the one macOS ships). Its quick tier runs each touched crate's suites
whole instead of mapping the diff to test fns - coarser, never less.
*.sh is pinned to LF so the shebang survives a Windows checkout.

Fixes #129

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
